; ===========================================================================
; npm configuration for the SSO test suite
; ===========================================================================
;
; legacy-peer-deps=true
; ---------------------
; Restores npm 6's peer-dependency resolution algorithm: peer-dep mismatches
; produce warnings instead of failing the install. Required because the AAP
; pins two packages whose published versions are upstream-incompatible at the
; peer-dependency layer:
;
;   - eslint@10.4.0 (AAP Section 0.6.1)
;   - eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@6.10.2 (AAP Section 0.6.1)
;
; eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@6.10.2 (the latest published release as of plan
; generation) declares:
;   peerDependencies: { "eslint": "^3 || ^4 || ^5 || ^6 || ^7 || ^8 || ^9" }
;
; The upstream plugin maintainers have not yet shipped a release that adds
; ESLint 10 to the peer range. Without `legacy-peer-deps=true` the bare
; `npm install` command documented in AAP Section 0.9.1 fails with
; `ERESOLVE could not resolve`, blocking onboarding for any developer or
; CI pipeline that follows the AAP verbatim.
;
; Setting the flag at the project level (this file) ensures every
; invocation of `npm install` — local, CI, or otherwise — automatically
; opts into the legacy resolver, so the AAP-documented command works as-is.
;
; Functional correctness is preserved: the active ESLint configuration is
; the flat config `eslint.config.js`, which loads `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y`
; via dynamic ESM import. ESLint 10 calls the plugin's exported rule
; functions identically to ESLint 9; the peer constraint is metadata, not
; a runtime gate. `npm run lint` exits 0 with zero warnings under this
; configuration (verified empirically — see the I1 QA Test Report's
; Edge Case #5 row).
;
; If a future release of eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y adds `^10` (or `>=10`) to
; its peer range, this file becomes redundant and can be safely deleted.
;
; Reference:
;   - https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/using-npm/config#legacy-peer-deps
;   - AAP Section 0.6.1 (Testing Dependencies)
;   - AAP Section 0.9.1 (Setup commands)
;   - QA Test Report I1 (Issue 1 resolution)
legacy-peer-deps=true
